say why a window did not become key

becomeKeyWindow and becomeMainWindow are gated separately in platformWindowActivated:, and CIDER_MAIN
already printed each of them when it ran. What it could not print was the DECISION, so a window that
became main and never became key looked like a defect with no visible cause.

It also could not tell that apart from platformWindowActivated: never running at all, which is what
was actually happening.

  CIDER_MAIN activated NSKVONotifying_MMWindow style=0xf visible=1 canKey=1 canMain=1 isMain=1
  CIDER_MAIN activated NSKVONotifying_IATitlebarWindow style=0x800f visible=1 canKey=1 canMain=1 isMain=1

AND IT CORRECTED A STANDING CLAIM. Task #189 recorded that iA Writer never becomes key, with grey
traffic lights through a whole run, as unexplained. With this line the absence is visible: on a run
with no TYPE step there is no activated line at all, and on a run that types there is one, and the
window becomes key. wtype creates the virtual keyboard when it STARTS, so before any typing the seat
advertises no keyboard and the compositor can give no surface keyboard focus. The rig, not the port.

--- a/AppKit/NSWindow.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSWindow.m
@@ -3867,6 +3867,16 @@
                               withObject: self];
 
     _isActive = YES;
+    /* THE TWO ANSWERS AND THE MASK THEY COME FROM. becomeKeyWindow and becomeMainWindow are gated
+     * separately here, so a window that becomes main and never becomes key is deciding it, and the
+     * decision is invisible from either side. An application may override either method. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_MAIN") != NULL) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_MAIN activated %s %p style=0x%lx visible=%d canKey=%d canMain=%d isMain=%d\n",
+                object_getClassName(self), (void *) self, (unsigned long) _styleMask,
+                (int) [self isVisible], (int) [self canBecomeKeyWindow],
+                (int) [self canBecomeMainWindow], (int) [self isMainWindow]);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
     if ([self canBecomeKeyWindow]) {
         [self becomeKeyWindow];
     }
